From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Opsero <noreply@opsero.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:44:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: xilinx: isppipeline: use the DT gain and threshold
 values

For the xlnx,isppipeline-1.0 core, xisp_parse_of() reads the required
xlnx,rgain, xlnx,bgain and xlnx,pawb properties into xisp->rgain,
xisp->bgain and xisp->pawb. The red_gain, blue_gain and threshold
controls are then created with fixed defaults (100, 350 and 512), and
v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup() applies those defaults through s_ctrl, which
overwrites the parsed values before the first stream-on. The device
tree values never reach the hardware.

Create these three controls with the parsed values as their defaults,
so the device tree sets the initial state and the controls report it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Opsero <noreply@opsero.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-isppipeline.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-isppipeline.c b/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-isppipeline.c
index ffc8a10..480435a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-isppipeline.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/xilinx/xilinx-isppipeline.c
@@ -2648,8 +2648,17 @@ static int xisp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(&xisp->ctrl_handler, ARRAY_SIZE(xisp_ctrls) +
 				       ARRAY_SIZE(xisp_ctrls_gamma_correct));
 		for (itr = 0; itr < ARRAY_SIZE(xisp_ctrls); itr++) {
-			v4l2_ctrl_new_custom(&xisp->ctrl_handler,
-					     &xisp_ctrls[itr], NULL);
+			struct v4l2_ctrl_config cfg = xisp_ctrls[itr];
+
+			/* Start from the values given in the device tree */
+			if (cfg.id == V4L2_CID_XILINX_ISP_RED_GAIN)
+				cfg.def = xisp->rgain;
+			else if (cfg.id == V4L2_CID_XILINX_ISP_BLUE_GAIN)
+				cfg.def = xisp->bgain;
+			else if (cfg.id == V4L2_CID_XILINX_ISP_THRESHOLD)
+				cfg.def = xisp->pawb;
+
+			v4l2_ctrl_new_custom(&xisp->ctrl_handler, &cfg, NULL);
 		}
 		for (itr = 1; itr < ARRAY_SIZE(xisp_ctrls_gamma_correct); itr++) {
 			v4l2_ctrl_new_custom(&xisp->ctrl_handler,
